          "prompt": "From: Buddy Williams <buddy.williams@insurity.com>\nSubject: State sync stuck in \"changed on multiple nodes\" conflict loop �� dashboard counts non-authoritative for 1h+\n\nBody:\nSummary\r\n\r\n  On my node (default / BO2LNXNEVO04 (QA), Refine 4.2.0, daemon on port 8082), state sync has been failing continuously since 2026-08-15T16:34:44Z. Every attempt (roughly\r\n  every minute) returns the same Conflict(\"Refine state changed on multiple nodes: ��\") error and the health record is not resetting. As a result the web dashboard shows the\r\n  banner:\r\n\r\n  �� State sync has failed since 2026-08-15T16:34:44Z. All-node counts are local and non-authoritative until synchronization recovers.\r\n\r\n  ��and the \"All\" tab counts (Backlog 0 / To do 83 / Plan 2 / Implement 5 / Quality 0 / Governance 0 / Review 34 / Done 788 / Failed 5 / Cancelled 3) are just this node's\r\n  local projection.\r\n\r\n  Impact\r\n\r\n  - Fleet-wide roll-up on the Dashboard is not authoritative �� it's the last known snapshot plus this node's local delta.\r\n  - This node's outbound state changes are not being published to origin/refine/state, so the other nodes can't see my work either.\r\n  - Reconciliation isn't self-healing; it's been failing for ~1h 45m with no forward progress.\r\n\r\n  Environment\r\n\r\n  - Refine version: 4.2.0, api_contract_version: 2, launch mode binary\r\n  - Daemon: port 8082, daemon_healthy: true, worker_state: idle, web_available: true, no degraded_integrations\r\n  - Active node: default �� BO2LNXNEVO04 (QA), target root /insurity/ProSuite, agent CLI claude\r\n  - Fleet (5 registered, all enabled): default, bo2lnxnevo03-buddy, bo2lnxnevo02-ethan, BO2LNXIPSAPP01, instance_jason\r\n  - Git remote configured, refine/state branch exists, state_sync_debounce_seconds=5, state_sync_stale_threshold_seconds=900\r\n\r\n  Timeline (all UTC)\r\n\r\n  �������������������������������������������������������������������Щ�������������������������������������������������������������������\r\n  ��             Field              ��              Value              ��\r\n  �������������������������������������������������������������������੤������������������������������������������������������������������\r\n  �� monitoring_since               �� 2026-08-15T11:56:38Z            ��\r\n  �������������������������������������������������������������������੤������������������������������������������������������������������\r\n  �� last_success_at                �� 2026-08-15T14:56:30Z            ��\r\n  �������������������������������������������������������������������੤������������������������������������������������������������������\r\n  �� stale_since                    �� 2026-08-15T15:11:30Z            ��\r\n  �������������������������������������������������������������������੤������������������������������������������������������������������\r\n  �� failure_since                  �� 2026-08-15T16:34:44Z            ��\r\n  �������������������������������������������������������������������੤������������������������������������������������������������������\r\n  �� last_attempt_at                �� 2026-08-15T17:34:57Z (deferred) ��\r\n  �������������������������������������������������������������������੤������������������������������������������������������������������\r\n  �� last_failure_at                �� 2026-08-15T17:34:52Z            ��\r\n  �������������������������������������������������������������������੤������������������������������������������������������������������\r\n  �� last_reminder_at               �� 2026-08-15T17:34:52Z            ��\r\n  �������������������������������������������������������������������੤������������������������������������������������������������������\r\n  �� revision                       �� 1891                            ��\r\n  �������������������������������������������������������������������੤������������������������������������������������������������������\r\n  �� aggregate_counts_authoritative �� false                           ��\r\n  �������������������������������������������������������������������ة�������������������������������������������������������������������\r\n\r\n  Same conflict error was logged both when the failure first appeared (event: sync_failed @ 16:34:44Z, severity error) and every retry since (event: sync_failure_reminder,\r\n  severity warn). The conflict path set has looked unchanged across attempts.\r\n\r\n  Error message\r\n\r\n  Refine state changed on multiple nodes: goals/00/000SZW2PEJWJEAJG7SV7W003/goal.json,\r\n  goals/00/000SZW328X2HP1WVK9V7W004/goal.json, goals/00/000SZW375SPJW874J5V7W005/goal.json,\r\n  �� ~44 goal.json paths visible in the message before it truncates with `��` ��\r\n  goals/00/000SZY3TFX61EASEZP��\r\n\r\n  Source (Refine checkout /insurity/refine):\r\n  - src/tools/host/git_sync/service.rs:213-218 �� first-pass reconciliation, returns RefineError::Conflict(\"Refine state changed on multiple nodes: {conflicts}\") after\r\n  state_conflicts(&base, &local, &remote_state, &resolved_paths) comes back non-empty.\r\n  - src/tools/host/git_sync/service.rs:295-306 �� same check on the push-retry path (\"��during push retry: {conflicts}\").\r\n\r\n  What's healthy vs. what's stuck\r\n\r\n  - git fetch origin refine/state succeeds; the local refine/state worktree at /insurity/ProSuite/.git/refine-state-worktree is up to date with origin/refine/state, working\r\n  tree clean, HEAD cf656a8519 Sync Refine state: 1 goal (2026-08-15 13:34:19 -0400). Other nodes' commits are landing on the branch fine �� this is not a\r\n  network/auth/push-permission problem.\r\n  - The rebase step in perform_sync succeeds (no rebase-abort log entries).\r\n  - The failure is exclusively at state_conflicts �� the reconciler classifies dozens of goal paths as changed-on-both-sides-since-base and the \"non-overlapping goal changes\"\r\n  merge step does not defuse them.\r\n  - Because the check returns Err before any commit/push, this node has not written a state commit since 14:56:30Z, so the divergence set grows monotonically as the daemon\r\n  keeps mutating the live store (3 goal-agent processes plus the main agent are visible in system status).\r\n\r\n  Hypothesis\r\n\r\n  The reconciler is deadlocked: every retry re-observes the same \"both sides changed since base\" set because\r\n\r\n  1. no commit is written on this node until the conflict clears, so base never advances, and\r\n  2. active work continues to mutate goals on this node's live store while other nodes keep pushing their own updates to refine/state, so both sides keep drifting from that\r\n  stale base.\r\n\r\n  reconcile_non_overlapping_goal_changes evidently doesn't consider these overlapping (same-path) writes mergeable, and there's no operator-facing \"accept remote for path X\"\r\n  / \"accept local\" / \"recompute base to current head\" recovery path exposed. fleet sync just re-enters the same reconciler.\r\n\r\n  Additional observations that may matter\r\n\r\n  - The error string is truncated with �� at what looks like a fixed budget in both the health file and the activity-log event details �� the operator can't see the full\r\n  - state-sync-health.json records last_attempt_outcome: \"deferred\" on the most recent attempt but last_failure_at was updated within the same second, which reads oddly �� is\r\n  deferred supposed to be a distinct terminal outcome from failed, or is the retry loop double-recording?\r\n  - fleet sync returns state: Running and never surfaces the underlying reconciler error to the caller (had to read state-sync-health.json and refine log query \"state sync\"\r\n  to see the actual cause).\r\n\r\n  Repro / diagnostics I can attach\r\n\r\n  - refine system status (JSON)\r\n  - refine node list (JSON �� includes the full state_sync_health block and per-node counts)\r\n  - refine log query \"state sync\" (sync_failed + repeated sync_failure_reminder entries)\r\n  - run/8082/state-sync-health.json\r\n  - git log/git status from /insurity/ProSuite/.git/refine-state-worktree\r\n  - Can run refine log bundle if you want a redacted support bundle.\r\n\r\n  What I'd like from you\r\n\r\n  1. A way for fleet sync (or a dedicated recovery command) to unstick this without manually editing state �� either by advancing base to the current reconciled head, or by\r\n  letting the operator pick a side per path.\r\n  2. Surface the reconciler error on the CLI (fleet sync currently reports only Running / a bare operation record).\r\n  3. Include the full conflict path list (or a pointer to a file with it) instead of truncating with �� �� for a fleet this size, \"�� 44 goals\" isn't enough to reason about\r\n  scope.\r\n  4. Consider whether reconcile_non_overlapping_goal_changes should treat certain kinds of goal.json edits (e.g. per-round appends, monotonically increasing revision fields)\r\n  as auto-mergeable so a busy multi-node fleet doesn't wedge like this.\r\n\r\n\r\n[cid:insurity-small2_2f81c33c-d951-4e5c-a467-1113541ca22c.jpg]\r\nBuddy Williams\r\nBuddy.Williams@insurity.com\r\n\r\n[cid:excellence2026signature(17b0688e-5473-4b74-96eb-a73f633f2c2f)_48407359-d77b-4967-95cd-277a32b50ebc.png]<https://insurity.com/excellence?utm_source=Email-Signature&utm_medium=Email&utm_campaign=Event-Excellence-2026>\r\n\r\n_____________________________________________________________________________________________________\r\n\r\nThe information contained in this e-mail message is intended only for the personal and confidential use of the intended recipient(s). This message may be an attorney-client communication and/or work product and as such is privileged and confidential. If the reader of this message is not the intended recipient or an agent responsible for delivering it to the intended recipient, you are hereby notified that you have received this document in error and that any review, dissemination, distribution, or copying of this message is strictly prohibited. If you have received this communication in error, please notify us immediately by e-mail, and delete the original message.\r\n_____________________________________________________________________________________________________\r\n~~~Insurity~~~",
